@node fjel
@unnumbered fj.el

This repo contains some basic functions for interacting with a Forgejo instance (such as @uref{https://codeberg.org, codeberg.org}) from within Emacs.

It doesn't interact with @samp{forge} / @samp{magit}@comma{} which don't implement Gitea/Forgejo support for now (though this will likely change@comma{} see @uref{https://github.com/magit/forge/discussions/771}). Nor does it attempt to follow their wonderful design.

It just aims to cover a few of the bread and butter functions that will save you switching to the browser 80% of the time.

@node install
@unnumbered install

@samp{fj.el} is available in @uref{https://elpa.nongnu.org/, ELPA}.

You can also just pull it from the repo with use-package/straight@comma{} such as:

@lisp
(use-package fj
  :straight (:type git :host codeberg "martianh/fj.el")
  :config
  (setq fj-user "martianh"))
@end lisp

