@node limitations
@unnumbered limitations

@menu
* performance::
* general design::
@end menu

@node performance
@unnumberedsec performance

Unfortunately @samp{fj.el} is pretty slow at loading issues/PRs with lots of comments and other timeline elements. The relevant code was recently re-written to be partly async@comma{} and the rendering of HTML in item bodies was recently overhauled@comma{} but the performance is still terrible. This leads me to believe it is actually to do with the Forgejo API (as for example@comma{} my abominable old rendering code worked for 100+ items with Lemmy@comma{} but couldn't do 30 items in a timely manner with Forgejo.)

There is a defcustom@comma{} @samp{fj-timeline-default-items}@comma{} with a default value of 15@comma{} meaning we load 15 timeline elements by default. If you find the performance is no problem on longer items@comma{} you can increase this value. (The default apart from this setting would be 30.)

@node general design
@unnumberedsec general design

@samp{fj.el} started out as a tiny package around my general use-case: working with repos I own and that have few if any collaborators and only one remote. Working with other repos was added later@comma{} and some workflows and commands still need adjusting in this regard. If you find @samp{fj.el} generates a lot of friction with your workflow@comma{} feel free to let me know. (It's not easy hacking in the vague direction what I imagine other people's workflows to be.)

@node contributions
@unnumbered contributions

Contributions are welcome@comma{} as is feedback about your needs.

Please PR into branch @samp{dev} (@samp{main} is for releases)@comma{} and let me know if you're hacking on something.

Currently the project has just evolved organically out of my own needs (and my own libraries)@comma{} which are likely different to yours.

